      "problem": "Evaluate $21 \\times \\dfrac{7}{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Interpreting the fraction as division, we can write our expression as:\n\n$$\n21\\times 7\\div 3\n$$\n\nWe can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $\\times 7$ and the $\\div 3{:}$\n\n$$\n21 \\div 3\\times 7\n$$\n\nExpressing the division as a fraction, we arrive at:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{21}{3}\\times 7\n$$\n\nWe now solve:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\dfrac{21}{3}}_{7}\\times 7 = 7\\times 7 = 49.\n$$",
